# Project Plan – ArchiveAI

## Week 1 – Project Setup & Core Development

**Weekly Goal:** Set up the project architecture, database, authentication, and frontend foundation so the team can begin implementing the main features.

**Weekly Progress Tracking:** By the end of this week, the project should have a working development environment, database schema, login system, UI layout, and basic search integration.

### Day 1 Tasks

* Set up the Python backend project.
* Initialize the GitHub repository.
* Configure the PostgreSQL database connection.
* Design the archive database schema.
* Create tables for articles, interviews, and footage notes.
* Create the React project.
* Install Tailwind CSS.
* Set up the basic folder structure and routing.

### Day 2 Tasks

* Implement secure user authentication with a login API.
* Implement password hashing.
* Create sample archive data.
* Write database scripts to populate PostgreSQL.
* Design and build the login page.
* Create the application layout with navigation.

### Day 3 Tasks

* Develop database models.
* Create API endpoints for archive document retrieval.
* Test database connectivity.
* Optimize sample data organization.
* Build the dashboard page.
* Create the search interface design.

### Day 4 Tasks

* Create the archive search API to search documents using keywords.
* Integrate backend APIs with the database.
* Validate returned search results.
* Connect the search bar to the backend API.
* Display search results in the frontend.

### Day 5 Tasks

* Test authentication and search APIs.
* Fix identified backend issues.
* Verify database integrity.
* Improve query performance for searching.
* Improve the dashboard UI.
* Ensure responsive layouts across devices.

---

## Week 2 – Feature Development & AI Integration

**Weekly Goal:** Complete the core search system, AI-powered search, source attribution, filtering, and search history.

**Weekly Progress Tracking:** By the end of this week, users should be able to search archives, filter results, view source information, and access saved search history.

### Day 6 Tasks

* Integrate the OpenAI API with the backend search workflow.
* Implement source attribution logic.
* Return article title, author, date, and document ID.
* Create the search results page.
* Design a clean and readable results layout.

### Day 7 Tasks

* Improve AI search accuracy by preparing document context before API requests.
* Develop APIs to support source attribution in search responses.
* Display source attribution details below every search result.

### Day 8 Tasks

* Develop backend APIs for filtering archive results by content type.
* Validate filtered search results.
* Ensure correct document retrieval.
* Build filter options for articles, interviews, and footage notes.

### Day 9 Tasks

* Create backend APIs to save and retrieve recent search history.
* Store search history records in PostgreSQL.
* Verify database consistency.
* Develop the search history section.
* Display previous searches.

### Day 10 Tasks

* Optimize backend search performance.
* Improve API response time.
* Test all backend features together.
* Resolve integration issues.
* Refine UI styling.
* Improve the overall user experience.

---

## Week 3 – Testing, Optimization & Deployment

**Weekly Goal:** Test all features, fix bugs, optimize performance, prepare documentation, and deploy the application.

**Weekly Progress Tracking:** By the end of this week, ArchiveAI should be fully functional, tested, documented, and ready for presentation.

### Day 11 Tasks

* Perform backend integration testing for authentication, search, and AI services.
* Validate source attribution accuracy across all archive documents.
* Test frontend pages.
* Fix interface inconsistencies.

### Day 12 Tasks

* Improve backend error handling.
* Add API validation for invalid requests.
* Optimize SQL queries.
* Improve overall database performance.
* Enhance responsiveness and accessibility of all frontend components.

### Day 13 Tasks

* Conduct API stress testing.
* Resolve performance bottlenecks.
* Verify search history and filtering functionality with different datasets.
* Complete final frontend polishing.
* Improve loading states.

### Day 14 Tasks

* Prepare backend deployment configuration.
* Configure production environment settings.
* Perform complete system testing.
* Document all resolved issues.
* Connect the production frontend with the deployed backend APIs.

### Day 15 Tasks

* Deploy the backend application.
* Verify all API endpoints.
* Perform a final database backup.
* Validate application reliability.
* Deploy the frontend application.
* Conduct final UI testing.
* Prepare the project demonstration.





